\n- Also has state_name, state_abbr, and other columns\n\nCensus:\n- Has POPESTIMATE2025 which is the 2025 population estimate\n- Has NAME column which should have \"United States\" or similar for the total\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Get the total farmers markets from the farmers_markets table\n2. Get the total US population from the census table (the US total row)\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n\nLet me first peek at the data to understand how to get the US total from the census data.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Let me peek at both datasets to understand their structure:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_0146XBrUDeU6gzojRBUU3s9A","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"census","compose":"source.limit(5).select('NAME', 'POPESTIMATE2025')"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01NNppuvhCrG5dibWkTY8RoS","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.limit(5)"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":377,"cacheRead":17897,"cacheWrite":1458,"totalTokens":19746,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0018850000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0017897000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.0018225,"total":0.005511200000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":163},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914405414,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77GkcPPDTMrGtf1KJLr","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_0146XBrUDeU6gzojRBUU3s9A","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"NAME\",\"POPESTIMATE2025\"\n\"United States\",341784857\n\"Northeast Region\",58042054\n\"New England\",15431980\n\"Middle Atlantic\",42610074\n\"Midwest Region\",69762666\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914411117},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01NNppuvhCrG5dibWkTY8RoS","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"state_name\",\"state_abbr\",\"farmers_markets\",\"csa_programs\",\"farm_stands\",\"snap_ebt_markets\",\"snap_ebt_pct\",\"organic_vendor_markets\",\"organic_pct\",\"markets_with_website\",\"website_pct\"\n\"California\",\"CA\",647,95,223,100,15.5,114,17.6,246,38.0\n\"New York\",\"NY\",555,156,272,41,7.4,45,8.1,283,51.0\n\"Pennsylvania\",\"PA\",426,102,886,18,4.2,43,10.1,226,53.1\n\"Minnesota\",\"MN\",390,62,80,101,25.9,14,3.6,148,37.9\n\"Illinois\",\"IL\",370,64,713,29,7.8,42,11.4,155,41.9\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914411117},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see that:\n1. The census table has a \"United States\" row with POPESTIMATE2025 = 341,784,857\n2. The farmers_markets table has individual state rows with a farmers_markets column\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Sum all the farmers_markets values from the farmers_markets table\n2. Get the US population from the census table\n3. Calculate the ratio per 100,000\n\nLet me create a build script that joins these two pieces of data and computes the metric. Actually, since I just need the US total population and the sum of all farmers markets, I could:\n- Get total farmers markets via aggregate on farmers_markets alias\n- Get US population via a filter on the census alias\n- Then compose them together in a metric\n\nLet me think about the best approach. According to the xorq-catalog skill, I should create a build script that reads both sources and joins them to create the metric. Let me do that.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I'll create a metric by building a script that reads both sources, gets the US total population, and sums all farmers markets:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01PpTpcVvDL2eFwK5Zvzs7QQ","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener(); _o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]; u.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"farmers_markets\", storage_options=so)\n\n# Read census data\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"census\", storage_options=so)\n\n# Aggregate farmers markets count across all states\n# and get US total population from census\ntotals = fact.aggregate(total_farmers_markets=fact.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\nus_pop = (ref.filter(ref.NAME == \"United States\")\n            .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\").mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join and compute per 100,000 metric\nexpr = (\n    totals.join(us_pop, totals.k == us_pop.k)\n      .mutate(farmers_markets_per_100k=totals.total_farmers_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select(\"total_farmers_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"farmers_markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":798,"cacheRead":19355,"cacheWrite":709,"totalTokens":20876,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0039900000000000005,"cacheRead":0.0019355000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.00088625,"total":0.00682575},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":219},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914411117,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77H9DgFcuf9YeYMkZmb","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01PpTpcVvDL2eFwK5Zvzs7QQ","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1278 bytes to .xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914419084},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me build this script and add it to the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01EKS